---
// Who makes Sleep Moore and how the sounds are made: the trust page for people and for search.
import GetApp from '../components/GetApp.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, graph, pageUrl, webPage } from '../data/schema';
import { EMAIL, SITE } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const url = pageUrl('/about/');
const title = 'About Sleep Moore: how the sounds are made | Sleep Moore';
const description = 'Who makes Sleep Moore and how: real recordings remastered into seamless loops, no account, no ads, no tracking, and free for good. How the sounds, stories and meditations are made.';
const about = { '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${url}#about`, url, name: 'About Sleep Moore', about: { '@id': `${SITE}/#org` } };
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <script is:inline slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={graph(webPage(url, 'About Sleep Moore', description), about, breadcrumbs(url, [['About', '/about/']]))} />
  <section class="page-head lib-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>One idea, done quietly.</h1>
      <p>Sleep Moore is a small, independent sleep sounds app. This is how it is made, and what it will never do.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose guide">
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>Most sleep apps are loud about being calm: a feed of courses, a streak to keep, a paywall before the first sound plays, and an account before any of it. We wanted the opposite. Open it, press play, and the room changes. Nothing to manage, nothing to sign up for.</p>

      <h2>How the sounds are made</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Real recordings.</b> Every nature sound, the rain, the sea, the fire, the crickets, is a recording, either our own or released into the public domain. The noise colours (<a href="/sounds/white-noise/">white</a>, <a href="/sounds/pink-noise/">pink</a>, <a href="/sounds/brown-noise/">brown</a> and <a href="/sounds/green-noise/">green</a>) are generated, because that is what noise is.</li>
        <li><b>No seam.</b> Each recording is cut, levelled and crossfaded end to start, then stored losslessly, so there is no click or gap at the loop point for your ear to catch on in the night. That is also why the app uses lossless files rather than MP3.</li>
        <li><b>Levelled to sit together.</b> Every sound is matched in loudness, so any three can be mixed without one jumping out.</li>
        <li><b>Softened where it matters.</b> The sharpest fire pops and the closest thunder are tamed, so nothing startles you awake.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Stories and meditations</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/stories/">night journeys</a> and <a href="/meditations/">meditations</a> are written for Sleep Moore and read slowly by one calm voice. Stories are deliberately uneventful: you are somewhere safe, something gentle happens, and nothing goes wrong. You can read the opening of every story and every word of every meditation on this site.</p>

      <h2>What we will not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>No account.</b> Your mixes and settings stay on your phone.</li>
        <li><b>No ads and no tracking.</b> No advertising code and nothing that follows you around. The only thing that leaves your phone is crash and performance diagnostics, which do not identify you, so we can fix problems. Details are in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><b>No paywall on what is there.</b> Everything in the app at launch is free and stays free. A later, optional Sleep Moore+ will only add new content.</li>
        <li><b>No promises we cannot keep.</b> Sleep sounds mask noise and make bedtime calmer. They do not cure insomnia, and we will not say they do. <a href="/guides/do-sleep-sounds-help/">What the research actually says</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>We read every message. Write to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> with questions, a sound you would like, or a story idea.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <GetApp />
</Base>
